WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.352
Anika: A heap snapshot might help. But taking one can pause this runtime.

2
00:00:05.352 --> 00:00:10.992
Lukas: It can need extra memory too. This host has very little spare capacity.

3
00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:16.728
Raj: Maybe start with process stats and logs. Those are much lighter.

4
00:00:16.728 --> 00:00:24.000
Priya: Just to confirm, no production snapshot without approval, right? Could throttling buy us time?

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.144
Hannah: Probably. First save the build identifier and the memory timeline.

6
00:00:30.144 --> 00:00:36.144
Anika: I'm on it. We'll take the snapshot in an isolated reproduction instead.

7
00:00:36.144 --> 00:00:42.528
Lukas: Use sanitized input. A snapshot can contain customer data and credentials.

8
00:00:42.528 --> 00:00:48.672
Priya: What's the ETA for the lightweight evidence? We can't wait for a full reproduction.

9
00:00:48.672 --> 00:00:54.672
Hannah: I'll keep an eye on free memory. Stop collection if it makes things worse.

10
00:00:54.672 --> 00:01:00.120
Raj: Two minutes. I'll save only the reviewed logs to restricted storage.

